Finally got an Elf with a good supply of food (10 rations :) down into the
Mines.  About the 6th level down, stepped on the blinding trap, but since
I had eaten a floating eye way back when, not a problem.  I proceeded to
knock off the creatures that were created by the trap, ignoring the messages/
Finally, all that was left (that I could tell) was a newt, when suddenly I
get 'It Hits!'  I had no clue where 'it' was, and after 4 wild shoots, I
bit the dust, due to the short sword that the invisible dwarf lord 
carried.

Wouldnt you think that the telepathy intrinsic would allow one to 'see' 
invisible creatures when one is blinded?  Also, ought it not allow one
also to sense the presence of invisible creatures if one is NOT blinded?

Of course, this implies that see invisible becomes useless once telepathy
is gained.  However, if this is the case, I do have a suggestion:  Add a
'sentient' flag to all the monsters.  If a monster is sentient, then when
invisible, it CAN be sensed, but if it is not sentient, (like that
invisible purple worm), then it cannot be sensed.

Furthermore, when one has telepathy, then sentient creature can be
detected across the entire screen, while non-sentient creatures can only
be detected at close range (ie ESP amulet).

Additionally, the sensing of invisible creatures can 'waver', or temperary
not work for a bit.  IE, 'Your concentration wanders, and you lose track
of <insert inv. monster here>', and base the chance of this off the
int and wis (25% base for nominal stats)

Just my $0.02 :)

